CLOSURE_CHECKS_CLASSIFIER_AUDIT: {
  "schema_version": 1,
  "migration_run_id": "274893c2-7895-4fb2-8644-16e05d91c71c",
  "snapshot_timestamp": "2026-05-21T18:32:34Z",
  "ticket_id": "3aaa-0238",
  "items": [
    {
      "original_text": "After onboarding completes, direct pushes to main are blocked \u2014 all changes must go through a pull request (the onboarding process itself may use an initial direct push to install the CI workflow before activating the Ruleset)",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 5,
        "rationale": "describes a durable system behavior (branch protection rule) that remains in effect after onboarding, phrased as ongoing enforcement"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "PRs require all CI status checks to pass before merging: lint, format, tests, and LLM-based code review; the LLM review check passes when the review completes with no findings at severity critical \u2014 it exits non-zero otherwise",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 5,
        "rationale": "describes a durable policy and system behavior for PR merging criteria that persists after implementation"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "CI runs checks as separate GitHub Actions jobs with needs: dependencies: a lint/format job, a tests job (needs lint), and an LLM review job (needs tests); expensive jobs only run when prior jobs pass",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes a durable structural property of the CI system's job dependencies and conditional execution behavior that persists after implementation"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "The LLM review CI job reads API keys from GitHub Secrets and model IDs from GitHub Variables; each of the 3 tiers (light, standard, frontier) has an independently configurable model ID variable; provider is hardcoded to Anthropic in this epic, with the variable naming convention supporting future provider additions",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes durable system configuration capability with independent model ID variables per tier and extensible naming convention for future providers"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "The /dso:onboarding skill configures the GitHub repository: (a) merges the CI workflow file to main first, (b) then creates the Ruleset via gh api POST with --input JSON, (c) with pre-flight checks for gh version and admin permissions \u2014 emitting a manual setup guide and continuing without the Ruleset if either check fails; (d) enables auto-merge on the repository",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "transitional",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes a sequence of one-time setup actions (merging files, creating resources, configuring settings) that occur during onboarding, not an ongoing system property"
      },
      "user_decision": "accept",
      "post_migration_section": "CC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "For the initial implementation, Anthropic/Claude is the only available LLM provider; the LLM review job includes a configurable timeout (default 10 minutes) and an admin Ruleset bypass actor (RepositoryRole actor_id 5) so PRs can still merge during provider outages",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes durable system properties (single provider, configurable timeout, admin bypass capability) that persist after implementation rather than one-time completion tasks"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "An E2E validation test exercises the full PR lifecycle: creates a test branch, pushes a change, creates a PR, verifies CI status checks appear, and asserts the PR cannot merge until checks pass and merges successfully after checks pass",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes a durable validation capability that the system should continuously support, even though it's framed as a test exercise"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "A `validate.sh --ci` job runs in the CI pipeline as a separate GitHub Actions job (needs: tests; runs in parallel with the LLM review job) and is included in the Ruleset's required-check list; the job passes only when `validate.sh --ci` exits 0",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes a durable property of the CI system's behavior and structure that persists after implementation, not a one-time task"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "`ticket-platform-matrix.yml` fires on every PR (path filter removed or broadened to any change under `plugins/dso/scripts/` or `plugins/dso/hooks/`); its three matrix legs (`linux-bash4`, `macos-bash3`, `alpine-busybox`) are each individually included in the Ruleset's required-check list",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes a durable configuration state where the workflow fires on specified paths and matrix legs are required checks, persisting beyond initial setup"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "A Linux-only test-job variant runs the test suite with `BASH_OPTS='-eo pipefail'` exported, is included in the Ruleset's required-check list, and surfaces SIGPIPE-class failures that macOS local development cannot reproduce",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes a durable system property (test job exists with specific configuration and serves as required check) that persists after implementation, not a one-time completion task"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    }
  ]
}
